WEBVTT

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:04.020
I still can't believe how well things are going!

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:07.270
Now you're a step closer to being the Student Council President.

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:09.740
But we haven't won the election yet!

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:12.320
We have to psych ourselves up with the camp tomorrow!

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.400
I'll do my best.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:15.780
Same here.

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:19.900
Good job today!

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:21.450
See you tomorrow!

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:24.460
See you later, Mii-chan, Aomi-san!

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:28.160
Hey, Yuuki...

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:28.860
Hm?

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:32.760
Could we stop by a convenience store?

00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:34.380
Sure.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:39.860
Something really good happened today, so...

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:41.310
Yep.

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:46.240
I'm sure Daiki-kun is happy for us.

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:46.920
Yeah.

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:30.460
All right, let's begin the camp!

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:35.320
First and foremost, Oojima-kun, congratulations on qualifying for the real election.

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:36.340
Thank you!

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:40.340
All of you performed excellently during the primaries.

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:43.840
However, this is just one step in the process.

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:45.850
There's much we still need to do.

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:48.570
We have an entire election ahead of us.

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:50.400
The real election will be even more demanding.

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:55.110
I want to make that perfectly clear to all of you right now.

00:02:55.830 --> 00:03:00.360
First, Oojima-kun received a little over 600 votes in the primaries.

00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:05.540
And these are the votes received by the other two candidates, Shinonome and Tatsumi.

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:09.860
What do you think?

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:13.290
You were already aware, but didn't want to think about it, right?

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:17.820
Did ignoring the numbers help you think that you'd already won?

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:23.080
With this, you should understand the harsh reality of our situation.

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:26.560
However, we shouldn't give up just because the odds are against us.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:29.000
It's so overwhelming, though.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:32.810
I can understand how you could feel that after seeing these numbers,

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:35.570
but these aren't the real numbers.

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:40.580
<i>These</i> are the real numbers.

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:43.220
The iron votes for each candidate.

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:44.320
"Iron votes"?

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:45.650
Yes.

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:49.080
The votes held by each party, which will not go to any other party.

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:52.900
Oojima-kun has 600,
the Finance Commission has 1,000,

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:56.520
and the General Affairs Commission has 1,400, for a total of 3,000.

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:58.560
These votes won't change, no matter what.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:00.720
My 600 are iron votes?

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:04.890
I think there are a lot of people who gave him the vote just for fun, though.

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:08.280
Given the situation, they may have.

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:14.000
However, even if it was for fun, the candidate they voted for passed the primaries.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:15.650
And rather dramatically, no less.

00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:20.900
Well, I think most people would want to keep supporting you after that.

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:22.840
There are 6,000 students.

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:25.640
If there are 3,000 iron votes in total,

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:28.740
the other 3,000 are swing votes.

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:32.900
You can easily get those 3,000 votes if you sway the voters.

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:33.790
Sway them?

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:36.170
That's right. Sway the voters.

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:38.400
People say that a lot...

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:40.170
...but how exactly do you sway them?

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:44.800
One hint lies in Shirakawa Ayame, the candidate who nearly qualified yesterday.

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:46.960
Shirakawa Ayame...

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:48.220
That's it!

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:52.440
I need to really get it out there that I'm not a part of any of the three commissions!

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:53.430
Precisely.

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:57.480
How would doing that sway people to vote for you?

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:01.700
In the end, the Finance and General Affairs Commissions are parts of the Student Council.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:04.940
In other words, their competition may look like infighting to some people.

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:07.180
Yuuki's different in that respect.

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:09.280
He's a complete outsider.

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:11.580
That alone paints him in an honorable light.

00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:15.580
Something like, "A third candidate trying to overturn the old order!"

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:19.160
That could really sway the voters!

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:22.590
This might work pretty well against Shinonome-san.

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:28.500
Indeed. Shinonome's campaign portrays her as a revolutionary.

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:32.720
However, she's also the Finance Commission candidate, a member of the Student Council.

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:38.360
What would happen if you also called yourself a revolutionary and competed against her?

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:42.640
Between a revolution led by a member of the old order

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:45.600
and a revolution by a fresh, new outsider,

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:47.110
the latter will make a much stronger impression!

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:50.240
And the voters will be swayed our way.

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:54.250
Yesterday, Shinonome was able to sway 1,700 swing votes.

00:05:54.890 --> 00:05:57.870
Where will those votes go today?

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:03.500
We should come up with a really catchy slogan.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:09.060
Man, that guy's a pro!

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:10.340
He's the real deal!

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:13.400
He really feels like a capable man.

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:14.880
He must be popular!

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:18.800
I hear 99 percent of the votes
he got were from girls!

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:22.110
We can't expect votes like that for Ooshima.

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:25.140
Cooking's the only thing he's got going for him.

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:26.960
Running your mouths like horses...

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:31.120
Girls love guys who can cook.
It's a worthwhile trait.

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:32.370
Huh? Really?

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:38.280
Yeah! I hope I can cook with my husband when I get married.

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:43.170
Making food together with the one you love sounds like so much fun!

00:06:45.410 --> 00:06:47.340
I cut my finger!

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:50.780
A-Are you okay, Yuu... ki...

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:55.540
Yuu-kun, is everything all...

00:06:55.540 --> 00:06:56.600
Yuu-kun?

00:06:58.290 --> 00:07:01.060
Wh-What are you doing?

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:02.610
Stopping the bleeding.

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:06.450
S-Stopping bleeding, huh?

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:12.490
Um, I don't think you have to suck his finger to stop the bleeding.

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:17.750
Really? I do this for my little brothers all the time.

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:20.940
Your little brothers?! That's Yuuki!

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:20.960
He's not your little broth—
Your little brothers?! That's Yuuki!

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:22.420
He's not your little broth—

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:33.970
Not... your little brother.

00:07:35.590 --> 00:07:36.810
How is it now?

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:37.430
What?

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:39.880
Did it stop bleeding?

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:42.680
Y-Yeah. I think it did.

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:45.940
That's great. Let me put a band-aid on it.

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:48.280
Th-Thanks.

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:53.000
Hey, Chisato!

00:07:54.610 --> 00:07:57.820
If you're all right now, get back to work.

00:07:57.820 --> 00:07:59.950
Yeah, I will.

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:07.840
Thanks for the food!

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:09.760
So? How did it taste?

00:08:10.190 --> 00:08:11.320
Normal...

00:08:12.390 --> 00:08:14.510
isn't the word. Good.

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:18.840
A perfect dish that hits the spot! Japanese-style curry done right!

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:20.430
It was very satisfying!

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:22.460
Thank you very much.

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:26.340
Oojima-senpai and I gave it our best, so I'm glad you enjoyed it!

00:08:27.350 --> 00:08:30.100
I'll do the dishes, so you guys go relax.

00:08:30.100 --> 00:08:32.610
Oh, no. That's my job, too.

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:35.200
Don't worry. You should get going.

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:37.370
You can't keep your little brothers waiting.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:40.850
We can handle this from here, so don't worry.

00:08:40.850 --> 00:08:42.120
Yuu-kun, you take a break, too.

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:43.240
Huh?

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:44.370
Are you sure?

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:47.750
Totally! We don't want you doing all the work.

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:51.170
Okay, then. Thank you very much!

00:08:57.870 --> 00:09:01.770
I never knew the campgrounds had an open-air bath!

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:05.190
Too bad the Food Club never had camps.

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:13.020
Yuuki!

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:15.520
Ch-Chisato?!

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:16.860
Are you alone?

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:18.030
Y-Yeah.

00:09:20.930 --> 00:09:21.500
What's up?

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:22.290
Whoa!

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:24.760
Hey, how did you open that door?

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:26.400
It wasn't locked.

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:38.220
Why are you acting so weird?

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:39.700
Look at me.

00:09:39.700 --> 00:09:41.320
I... uh...

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:43.720
I'm the one who barged in.

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:46.180
There's no need to be shy.

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:47.810
Yeah, but...

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:56.040
We took baths together a lot when we were little.

00:09:56.040 --> 00:09:59.360
When we were little, yeah. Things are different now.

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:01.340
Only because you didn't like it.

00:10:01.340 --> 00:10:02.440
Well, yeah.

00:10:04.190 --> 00:10:05.960
Does it still bother you?

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:08.330
Well, I...

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:13.020
Why are you here?

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:14.120
No reason.

00:10:14.120 --> 00:10:15.680
"No reason"?

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:17.970
I don't need a reason to be here.

00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:22.420
What's the matter?

00:10:23.210 --> 00:10:24.560
Don't you get it?

00:10:28.210 --> 00:10:30.600
We should probably get out of the bath now.

00:10:31.510 --> 00:10:32.880
We might get dizzy.

00:10:34.390 --> 00:10:37.000
Why don't you do anything?

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:37.490
What?

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:41.880
Don't you want to touch me?

00:10:42.590 --> 00:10:46.000
Don't you want to look at my naked body?

00:10:48.110 --> 00:10:49.300
Tell me.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:55.100
Yuuki-senpai, are you there?

00:10:55.100 --> 00:10:56.630
Nope! There's nobody here!

00:10:58.110 --> 00:11:00.220
Then I'm coming in.

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:02.220
W-Wait a second!

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:04.700
What's wrong?

00:11:04.700 --> 00:11:06.390
We're both guys.

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:09.770
Well, there are still problems with that...

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:10.390
Huh?

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:18.320
Oh, you look ready to go!

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:20.180
This isn't what it looks like!

00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:23.760
Dummy.

00:11:33.950 --> 00:11:37.940
Seriously... I can't even get any peace and quiet in the bath?

00:11:37.940 --> 00:11:39.090
Why?!

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:40.800
Why won't you go?

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:42.470
Because I don't need to go.

00:11:43.070 --> 00:11:45.400
It's the anniversary of our mother's death!

00:11:45.400 --> 00:11:48.140
Just do it with the rest of the family.

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:51.640
What's your problem with the family?

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:55.770
You should ask <i>her</i> that, not me.

00:11:56.570 --> 00:11:59.490
Don't talk about your own mother that way!

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:03.380
Oh, Yuu-kun!

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:07.240
He caught us arguing, Satsuki.

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:11.040
Sorry. I didn't mean to eavesdrop.

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:13.500
You don't need to apologize.

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:15.750
It's our fault for talking in a place like this.

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:18.050
I'm really sorry.

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:22.800
If you keep apologizing,
I might call you Bowjima again.

00:12:24.050 --> 00:12:26.560
Oh, you two are pretty close, aren't you?

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:28.600
But I won't let you flirt with other girls.

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:30.430
You already kissed me, after all!

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:33.500
Come on, Hazuki-sensei!

00:12:34.910 --> 00:12:36.600
See you!

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:40.280
U-Um...

00:12:48.550 --> 00:12:50.960
Just how many alarm clocks do you need?

00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:55.370
I only brought ten today, but I use plenty more back home.

00:12:55.850 --> 00:13:00.840
I might not be able to wake up, so I'm counting on you if that happens.

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:01.860
Counting on me for what?

00:13:01.860 --> 00:13:05.510
You know what to do when someone won't wake up.

00:13:08.570 --> 00:13:10.500
An elbow to the solar plexus?

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:13.660
Man, relax. I was just joking.

00:13:13.660 --> 00:13:16.150
Your jokes are too sick!

00:13:17.710 --> 00:13:19.660
Good night, Senpai.

00:13:19.660 --> 00:13:21.070
Night.

00:13:25.330 --> 00:13:27.780
I knew I should've brought it.

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:31.920
What is it now? You can't sleep on a different pillow?

00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:34.240
That's exactly right.

00:13:34.240 --> 00:13:38.520
Oh, I know. Could you become my pillow?

00:13:38.520 --> 00:13:40.480
You can't use my arm as your pillow.

00:13:40.480 --> 00:13:43.660
No, my pillow is a hug pillow.

00:13:43.660 --> 00:13:44.260
Huh?

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:47.000
Hey, stop!

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:49.620
Let me go!

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:50.820
It's no use.

00:13:50.820 --> 00:13:53.220
I've got you in a joint lock.

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:55.500
I'm a black belt.

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:57.770
Black belt? In what?

00:13:57.770 --> 00:13:59.980
You feel so nice!

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:03.380
It feels just like my hug pillow back home.

00:14:04.090 --> 00:14:06.360
I think I might be able to fall asleep now.

00:14:07.070 --> 00:14:09.380
Hey, Yume? Yume!

00:14:10.630 --> 00:14:11.660
Seriously?

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:16.920
Hey, Yume, wake up!

00:14:16.920 --> 00:14:18.780
I need to use the bathroom!

00:14:18.780 --> 00:14:20.060
Hey, Yume!

00:14:20.570 --> 00:14:23.280
I'll never let you go.

00:14:25.790 --> 00:14:28.720
I guess he didn't bring
ten alarm clocks for nothing.

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:31.560
Oh no! I can't hold it in anymore!

00:14:31.560 --> 00:14:33.680
I didn't want to do this...

00:14:34.610 --> 00:14:36.320
Thank you, thank you!

00:14:36.320 --> 00:14:40.040
It's your candid candidate, Tatsumi Moheiji!

00:14:43.670 --> 00:14:44.860
All right.

00:14:47.350 --> 00:14:50.360
Now where should I sleep tonight?

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:53.650
It might be dangerous to go back to the club room.

00:14:53.650 --> 00:14:54.370
Huh?

00:14:56.010 --> 00:14:57.370
That's...

00:14:59.650 --> 00:15:00.750
Sensei!

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:02.370
Huh?

00:15:02.370 --> 00:15:04.920
Oh, it's you, Yuu-kun!

00:15:08.070 --> 00:15:09.390
Yuu-kun!

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:11.460
Whoa, Sensei!

00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:14.940
Hey, let's kiss!

00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:15.920
I want a kiss!

00:15:15.920 --> 00:15:15.940
I don't!
I want a kiss!

00:15:15.940 --> 00:15:17.320
I don't!

00:15:17.320 --> 00:15:20.420
Cheap-ass. Wanna drink together, then?

00:15:20.420 --> 00:15:21.270
No.

00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:24.560
You don't even have anything left.

00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:27.280
Come on. Let's get back to the campsite.

00:15:28.790 --> 00:15:30.280
We're here, Sensei.

00:15:30.910 --> 00:15:33.030
You can get back inside on your own, right?

00:15:33.030 --> 00:15:35.700
I can't go back!

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:38.830
But guys aren't allowed beyond this point.

00:15:39.210 --> 00:15:41.480
It's all right!

00:15:50.030 --> 00:15:51.100
I'm inside...

00:15:51.100 --> 00:15:53.620
Take me to my room!

00:15:53.620 --> 00:15:54.720
Shh!

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:03.800
I can't eat any more...

00:16:06.550 --> 00:16:08.700
Yuu-kun, where are you touching?

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:12.030
Sh! You're gonna wake everybody up!

00:16:14.530 --> 00:16:16.700
Good night, Sensei.

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:20.200
Yeah, nighty night.

00:16:30.070 --> 00:16:31.420
Pervert!

00:16:31.930 --> 00:16:35.180
There's a pervert on the loose! Someone help!

00:16:35.600 --> 00:16:36.860
Wait!

00:16:36.860 --> 00:16:38.860
Don't let him get away!

00:16:41.910 --> 00:16:43.690
Hold it!

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:46.710
Get him!

00:16:53.850 --> 00:16:55.060
Shit!

00:17:04.190 --> 00:17:05.440
What's the matter?

00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:09.480
Excuse us. A pervert may be hiding somewhere around here.

00:17:09.480 --> 00:17:11.480
Did you see anyone?

00:17:11.480 --> 00:17:13.720
No, I don't know anything about this.

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:15.810
I see.

00:17:15.810 --> 00:17:17.700
Did he do anything?

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:19.470
No, not that we know of.

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:22.920
Then you might want to keep it down.

00:17:22.920 --> 00:17:25.500
Many of the girls are asleep.

00:17:25.500 --> 00:17:29.860
For now, go around and tell everyone to lock their doors.

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:31.860
Okay, we will!

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:33.780
Good night, then.

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:35.860
Sorry for disturbing you.

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:37.600
Where did he go?

00:17:37.600 --> 00:17:39.860
Let's try downstairs.

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:42.420
You can come out now.

00:17:45.610 --> 00:17:47.200
Um, thanks.

00:17:47.200 --> 00:17:48.880
You saved me.

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:51.660
You're not exactly in the clear yet,

00:17:51.660 --> 00:17:52.590
Outlawjima-kun.

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:55.760
Outlawjima? I'm a criminal now?

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:57.260
Naturally.

00:17:57.260 --> 00:18:02.200
You were guilty the moment you stepped into the girls' campsite, with its strict no-men policy.

00:18:02.200 --> 00:18:04.920
Then why did you save me?

00:18:04.920 --> 00:18:10.480
Knowing you, I'm sure you have your reasons for being here.

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:11.770
Shinonome-san...

00:18:12.310 --> 00:18:16.280
So go ahead and explain what happened.

00:18:18.170 --> 00:18:19.280
I see.

00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:22.860
I'm sorry my sister dragged you into this mess.

00:18:22.860 --> 00:18:25.660
Don't be. I'm satisfied just knowing you understand.

00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:29.340
But something is still bugging me.

00:18:29.340 --> 00:18:30.380
What is it?

00:18:30.910 --> 00:18:34.590
Why are you so close to my sister?

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:36.010
Huh?

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:41.940
A student normally wouldn't carry
a drunk teacher all the way to her room.

00:18:41.940 --> 00:18:44.770
Well... she <i>is</i> our club advisor.

00:18:45.230 --> 00:18:50.480
You still could've called a girl in the club and avoided this entire mess.

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:57.050
I'm starting to believe that the two of you have a special relationship.

00:18:57.050 --> 00:18:58.100
Is that strange?

00:18:58.100 --> 00:18:59.400
It is!

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:02.720
There's nothing going on between us!

00:19:02.720 --> 00:19:03.760
Is that a fact?

00:19:03.760 --> 00:19:05.280
Yes, it is!

00:19:05.280 --> 00:19:09.080
If I find out you're lying, I'll disclose what happened tonight to the public.

00:19:09.450 --> 00:19:10.750
Are you threatening me?

00:19:11.110 --> 00:19:13.750
I just want to know the truth.

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:19.200
Then let me ask you another question.

00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:25.040
I'll pretend all this never happened if you answer me truthfully.

00:19:25.820 --> 00:19:27.180
Fine.

00:19:27.990 --> 00:19:32.400
All right. Did you kiss my sister?

00:19:33.090 --> 00:19:34.860
Tell me the truth.

00:19:37.030 --> 00:19:39.380
I-I did.

00:19:39.380 --> 00:19:41.420
I knew it.

00:19:41.420 --> 00:19:44.460
But that was an accident!

00:19:44.460 --> 00:19:45.870
What's that supposed to mean?

00:19:46.210 --> 00:19:51.120
Well, just like today, Sensei was dead drunk.

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:52.880
She caught me off guard.

00:19:52.880 --> 00:19:58.380
So you're saying that my sister forced you into kissing, right?

00:20:00.870 --> 00:20:02.880
I wouldn't go so far as to say that.

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:06.640
I see. I get it now, more or less.

00:20:06.640 --> 00:20:08.480
You do?

00:20:08.480 --> 00:20:14.150
Yes. I understand why you care about her more than a normal student would.

00:20:14.510 --> 00:20:15.140
Huh?

00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:21.570
My sister forces you to do things from time to time, doesn't she?

00:20:22.330 --> 00:20:24.820
And you're not against it at all.

00:20:25.270 --> 00:20:30.040
You tell yourself you don't have a choice and just put up with it.

00:20:30.040 --> 00:20:31.160
Am I right?

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:35.120
Moreover, because of that kiss,

00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:38.090
you can't leave her when she's dead drunk.

00:20:38.750 --> 00:20:40.960
You're worried about what she might do.

00:20:42.430 --> 00:20:46.510
In the end, you care about my sister.

00:20:46.910 --> 00:20:49.140
I don't hate her, obviously.

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:52.040
But I'm not in love with her, either.

00:20:52.040 --> 00:20:53.640
All right.

00:20:54.830 --> 00:20:58.360
As promised, I'll let tonight's incident slide.

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:00.150
Thanks so much.

00:21:00.870 --> 00:21:03.290
Then I'll be going now.

00:21:03.290 --> 00:21:07.140
I think those girls are still patrolling the hallways. Are you sure you want to?

00:21:08.890 --> 00:21:12.300
You should wait here for an hour or so for things to settle down.

00:21:12.300 --> 00:21:15.540
But then I'd be bothering you even more.

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:18.340
Then how about you do
something for me in return?

00:21:18.340 --> 00:21:20.840
Something in return?

00:21:21.190 --> 00:21:25.840
Yes. That way you'll be able to stay here without feeling sorry.

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:28.030
You have a point.

00:21:28.030 --> 00:21:30.350
But what should I...

00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:52.240
Yuu-kun, you jerk.

00:22:18.730 --> 00:22:23.530
In the classroom, looking out the window,
kyoushitsu no madobe de nagameru

00:22:23.530 --> 00:22:27.490
Watching the sky fade softly into twilight,
yasashii yuugure no sora

00:22:27.490 --> 00:22:31.630
I turn around, and there you are again
furimukeba kimi ga egao de

00:22:31.630 --> 00:22:35.710
Looking at me, you smile
kocchi wo miteta

00:22:35.710 --> 00:22:40.050
"Let's go home," you always say,
issho ni kaerou itsumo no

00:22:40.050 --> 00:22:44.210
Going all the places we go every day
toomawari wo shinagara

00:22:44.300 --> 00:22:48.240
Your fingers are just a step away
mada sukoshi todokanai

00:22:48.240 --> 00:22:54.720
But deep inside me, it hurts not holding your hand
yubisaki ga tada setsunakute

00:22:56.350 --> 00:23:01.360
In my heart, I found all these hopes and dreams
ano hi kimi to meguriaeta kara

00:23:01.360 --> 00:23:05.530
Because on that day we happened to meet
takusan no yume wo mitsuketan da

00:23:05.530 --> 00:23:07.720
Even when I wanted to cry,
nakitai toki demo

00:23:07.720 --> 00:23:11.420
You always stayed right there by my side
itsumo soba ni ite kurete

00:23:11.420 --> 00:23:13.950
I want to thank you so much
doumo arigatou

00:23:13.950 --> 00:23:18.210
What I wrote on that page I hid from you
no-to ni kaita himitsu no pe-ji wa

00:23:18.210 --> 00:23:22.090
Were the words that I just couldn't say
zutto iezu ni ita kotoba

00:23:22.090 --> 00:23:27.850
Now they float forever as whispers on the wind
ima kaze no naka zutto sasayaku yo nee

00:23:27.850 --> 00:23:35.720
Listen close, it says, "I love you so much"
kiite kimi ga daisuki da yo

00:23:41.650 --> 00:23:45.230
I prefer Western confectionery when it comes to sweets.

00:23:45.230 --> 00:23:48.110
But they're so high in calories.

00:23:48.110 --> 00:23:51.220
They come in countless variations and vibrant colors.

00:23:51.220 --> 00:23:54.180
They contain a lot of neutral lipids from stuff like butter and milk, too!

00:23:54.180 --> 00:23:57.540
With so many spices and fruits that aren't used in Japanese sweets!

00:23:57.540 --> 00:24:00.340
That's why some Japanese people don't care much for them.

00:24:00.340 --> 00:24:02.710
Anyway, Western sweets, Western sweets...

00:24:03.490 --> 00:24:06.460
Next time, Episode 8: "Truth!"

00:24:06.460 --> 00:24:08.550
Western sweets are made of dreams!

00:24:08.550 --> 00:24:09.920
You called?
